# The build context is an allowlist: everything is excluded unless it is re-included below, so a
# new local file (a credential, an index, a cache, an evaluation output) can never reach the image
# by default. Docker matches these patterns from the context root; the last matching line wins.
*

# Everything the image is built from (see the Dockerfile COPY lines).
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src/
!configs/
!prompts/
!scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh
!scripts/healthcheck.py

# Full release validation recomputes the committed source hashes at container startup. Re-include
# the parent directories explicitly (Docker cannot re-include a file below an ignored parent), then
# only the canonical Markdown source directory. Generated chunks, indexes, evaluations and every
# other workstation data path remain excluded by the leading allowlist rule.
!data/
!data/02_clean_markdown/
!data/02_clean_markdown/*.md

# Local state that can sit inside an allowed directory. `**/` is required: a bare
# `__pycache__/` only matches at the context root, which is how compiled files from a developer
# workstation reached an earlier image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
